// @check
// @error-at 12:11 no method '.frobnicate' on string
// @error-at 13:11 no method '.reverse' on string
// D1230's CONTROL for the string receiver, now that std is always a candidate (D3122):
// `frobnicate` is no module's export, and `reverse` is `std:array`'s over a list, which
// a string does not fit. Both keep the plain sentence.
//
// The pair is what makes the suggestion falsifiable. Without it, an enrichment
// that fired on every unresolved string method, or on every same-named std export
// whatever its receiver, would pass the positive fixtures
// (`tests/cases/std/ufcs-not-imported-cold-std.vl`) and this file would be the only
// thing to notice — which is exactly the widening the `ufcs-not-imported` code must not do.
print("ab".frobnicate())
print("ab".reverse())
